Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||02-01-2001||10:43 PM||||These are my Custom round headlights.. Fierolisa thinks it looks like a miata.. The conversion cost me $50 total<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/round.jpg"> <P>Dare to be different....<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula 18||02-01-2001||11:19 PM||||I like them. I have always like the look of round headlights. <BR>Can you tells us more about the how-to of the conversion. Also how's the new light patteren, is visibilty any better/worse?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Slammed Fiero||02-01-2001||11:31 PM||||I had original headlights on my car , so vision increased dramatically, There from a early 70's ford f-150 , the buckets have to be modified , but I have a mold in progress to make a new set of buckets out of fiberglass.... <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||02-01-2001||11:37 PM||||Very sharp... looks way better than a Miata, IMO.  I like the unique look.  Is it easy to switch back to the rectangulars, if you change your mind, or just want a different look?<P>Anyway, if you want something like a Miata -I mean, you can't hardly get a decent Miata for $50!  Nice idea  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     ||||reg||6
Z||000004||stimpy||02-02-2001||12:56 AM||||VERY COOL!<P>Please keep us updated on the possibility of easily reproducing this look. I think it looks(.)(.)||||reg||14
Z||000005||rogergarrison||02-02-2001||01:31 AM||||I thought about doing that too Jonathan. It is the way Ferrari 308s are-but I just got tired of the pop ups and wanted a sleeker look. Thats the reason I went to flush instead. Mine look better in person than they look in pics. Lisa says same thing. Did you use bulb from single or dual headlite system?||||reg||1
Z||000006||loafer87gt||02-02-2001||10:34 AM||||I posted a question on the Fiero digest when I first got my car about whether there was a way to get the dual round headlights like on a Testarossa, and a guy who had done a kit car replied that you can use the headlight assembly from a mid eighties VW Golf. Is this what all kit cars use for headlight assemblies?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||02-02-2001||10:49 AM||||I can switch back to the factory square units in a matter of minutes, no drilling/ molesting. I wanted dual rounds on my car , but it's a future project. These are dual Beam headlights, I have a source where I can switch them to the BMW like ION blue bulbs. For dual rounds I was looking at motor cycle units but found the cost wasn't worth it. The picture doesn't show the bezel that goes around the light. I used factory bezels and remoded the front to be round instead of square , then painted them body color...looks a little cleaner. The headlights themselves just plugged right in.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
